        "original_id": "001b4ea9-7d62-5737-94a2-28b02da38aaa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giacomo Meyerbeer, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n- Works: L'esule di Granata, Serenade No. 6 for Orchestra in D major K. 239, Serenata notturna\n- Places: Salzburg\n- Roles: opera composer, composer\n- Topics: Classical era, nineteenth-century stage composition, opera\n\nFacts:\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was born on 27 January 1756 and was baptised as Johannes Chrysostomus Wolfgangus Theophilus Mozart.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was a prolific and influential composer of the Classical era.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart wrote the Serenade No. 6 for Orchestra in D major K. 239, also called \"Serenata notturna,\" in Salzburg in 1776.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer was born as Jacob Liebmann Beer on 5 September 1791.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer was a German opera composer of Jewish birth and has been described as perhaps the most successful stage composer of the nineteenth century.\n- L'esule di Granata, meaning \"The exile of Granada,\" is a melodramma serio in two acts by Giacomo Meyerbeer.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer died on 2 May 1864.",
